{"qid":"Q2429397","names":["Carthage"],"title":"Carthage","endonym":{"native":"𐤒𐤓𐤕𐤟𐤇𐤃𐤔𐤕","lang":"phn"},"capsule":"Carthage was a Phoenician colonial city-state founded, according to tradition, around 814 BC near modern Tunis, which grew into the dominant commercial and naval power of the western Mediterranean. At its peak in the fourth and third centuries BC, the Carthaginian state controlled a maritime empire spanning coastal North Africa, Sardinia, part of Sicily, and the Iberian coast, governed by elected suffetes and a powerful merchant oligarchy. The three Punic Wars against Rome (264-241, 218-201, 149-146 BC) progressively dismantled Carthaginian power; Hannibal Barca's Italian campaign (218-203 BC) came close to destroying Rome but ultimately failed, and the Third Punic War ended with Roman general Scipio Aemilianus razing the city in 146 BC. The dataset attests the polity from 650 BC to 145 BC, consistent with its period as an identifiable power.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Carthaginian territorial control is moderately attested; core Tunisian territory and treaty-delimited zones with Rome are documented in ancient sources (Polybius, Livy), but inland African frontiers and fluctuating control in Iberia and Sicily are reconstructed from indirect evidence and remain conjectural in places.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Carthage","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Carthage-ancient-city-Tunisia"},{"label":"Livius.org: Punic Carthage","url":"https://www.livius.org/articles/place/carthage"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Ancient Carthage","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Carthage"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Ancient Carthage","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Dido (legendary founder)","nativeName":"𐤀𐤋𐤉𐤔𐤁𐤏𐤋","roman":"Elissa / Dido","start":-814,"end":-760,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Mago I","nativeName":"𐤌𐤂𐤍","roman":"Māgōn","start":-550,"end":-530,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Hasdrubal I (son of Mago)","nativeName":"𐤏𐤆𐤓𐤁𐤏𐤋","roman":"Hazrubaʿal I","start":-530,"end":-510,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Hamilcar I (Magonid)","nativeName":"𐤇𐤌𐤋𐤊𐤓𐤕","roman":"Ḥimilkart I","start":-510,"end":-480,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Himilco I","nativeName":"𐤇𐤌𐤋𐤊","roman":"Ḥimilkō I","start":-480,"end":-465,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Hanno I the Great","nativeName":"𐤇𐤍𐤀","roman":"Ḥannōʾ I","start":-465,"end":-440,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Gisco I","nativeName":"𐤂𐤓𐤔","roman":"Gēršōn I","start":-440,"end":-410,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Hannibal I (Magonid)","nativeName":"𐤇𐤍𐤁𐤏𐤋","roman":"Ḥannibaʿal I","start":-410,"end":-406,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Himilco II","nativeName":"𐤇𐤌𐤋𐤊","roman":"Ḥimilkō II","start":-406,"end":-396,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Mago II (Magonid)","nativeName":"𐤌𐤂𐤍","roman":"Māgōn II","start":-396,"end":-375,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Himilco III","nativeName":"𐤇𐤌𐤋𐤊","roman":"Ḥimilkō III","start":-375,"end":-368,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Hanno II the Great","nativeName":"𐤇𐤍𐤀","roman":"Ḥannōʾ II","start":-368,"end":-340,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Gisco II","nativeName":"𐤂𐤓𐤔","roman":"Gēršōn II","start":-345,"end":